The @RobinHoodCrypto NFT scene kept moving with continuous spaces, holder-focused utilities shipping in public, a playtest, an active auction, and several established communities tightening supply or expanding access. A lot of the activity still runs through overlapping holder groups rather than one dominant narrative.

A quick look at some of what’s been moving with #RobinRecap 

@TheSuitedApes remains one of the more established collections on the chain. Community attention continues to center on the Mutant drop expected this month, with holders set to receive free Mutants based on their holdings. The team has been teasing the pairing utility between Suited Apes and Mutants to unlock Jungle Brokers, which is framed as access to an expanding set of RWA, tokenized stocks and ETFs, tokenized real estate, and related tools. Whale activity, including from @crypto_czar_eth, has stayed visible across the collection and related projects.

@PrimalApesRH ran a multiplayer playtest for Primal Ball on November 7. The game is a 3D ape-style experience and required holding at least one Primal Ape to join. The team shared a play link and multiplayer lobby during the session, continuing a pattern of building and testing in public with the existing holder base. The Primal Apes spiked in volume last week, saw a new ATH and holders took profit.

@CompanionsWfit closed its first 1/1 auction (art by @inkartluis) with a winning bid of 0.5 ETH after 17 bids. The team has already pointed to another live drawing session and a follow-up auction. At the same time they continue preparing the broader Labyrinth Companions free mint, which is tied to quests in the WFit app so holders can earn mint access through activity in the existing product.

@vampsonchain has kept building around utility. Bloodbath soft-staking (signature only, NFT stays in the wallet) remains live with BLOOD points for games plus a share of royalties paid in ETH on 31-day cycles. Collabs have expanded the system so other collections can also stake, with royalty streams shared between the communities. Tenvek, the native video editor and compositor built by the founder, is in alpha for Vamp holders on Windows and Mac, with planned revenue share flowing back into the staking pool. Multiple collabs for guaranteed or first-come mint spots have also run.

@RealCashpig and the StreetHood crew continue running near-continuous 24/7 spaces that function more as an ongoing community hub than a standard scheduled discussion. People drop in for market updates, early mint and access talk, light conversation, and general engagement across the chain’s NFT projects. Giveaways and pinned spaces remain common, and the format has stayed consistent even as individual collections move in and out of focus. The Cash Grab collection (the collaboration between Cash Pig and @pixelord) is still waiting on its full reveal, keeping it on the radar for the same community that has been following the spaces and related drops.

@VaultlingsNFT (2,965 supply) has been leaning into its @BankFiOfficial connection, with creator royalties used to buy units tied to bitcoin mining and World Mobile. They discussed a deal with @1000PassNFT committing 50% of royalties to the same verticals, while Crypto Czar engaged with “You’re all getting a raise.” The account kept its usual dry workplace-humor posts.

